---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Instruments" currentPath="/instruments">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Entry</a> / System / Instruments
  </div>

  <h1>Instruments</h1>
  <p class="page-meta">Calibration tools for validating design intent · Updated February 2026</p>

  <div class="content-section">
    <p>
      Instruments are validation tools that measure coherence between declared intent and observable execution. They do not judge taste. They judge honesty—whether a design honors the principles it claims to follow.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each instrument asks a specific, answerable question. The verdict is binary or ternary: PASS, CAUTION, or BREACH. No scores. No optimization. Only alignment.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="instruments-list">
    <article class="instrument-card">
      <div class="instrument-header">
        <div class="instrument-number">I01</div>
        <h2><a href="/instruments/contrast-validator">Contrast Validator</a></h2>
      </div>
      <p class="instrument-description">
        Measures contrast ratios against declared intent. Not accessibility alone—but whether contrast serves the stated philosophy. Authority requires clarity. Restraint permits subtlety. The validator checks if contrast matches intent.
      </p>
      <div class="instrument-status">Available</div>
    </article>

    <article class="instrument-card">
      <div class="instrument-header">
        <div class="instrument-number">I02</div>
        <h2><a href="/instruments/emphasis-counter">Emphasis Counter</a></h2>
      </div>
      <p class="instrument-description">
        Identifies competing focal points within a composition. A single entry point is structural necessity. Multiple emphases produce ambiguity. The counter detects whether attention is directed or scattered.
      </p>
      <div class="instrument-status">Available</div>
    </article>

    <article class="instrument-card">
      <div class="instrument-header">
        <div class="instrument-number">I03</div>
        <h2>Spacing Auditor</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="instrument-description">
        Verifies that spacing follows consistent mathematical ratios. Arbitrary spacing produces visual discord. Systematic spacing creates rhythm. The auditor checks if intervals are intentional or accidental.
      </p>
      <div class="instrument-status coming-soon">Coming soon</div>
    </article>

    <article class="instrument-card">
      <div class="instrument-header">
        <div class="instrument-number">I04</div>
        <h2>Hierarchy Checker</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="instrument-description">
        Answers one question: Does the eye know where to start? Hierarchy is not taste—it is perceptual physics. The checker validates that visual emphasis matches informational importance.
      </p>
      <div class="instrument-status coming-soon">Coming soon</div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="instruments-note">
    <h3>Methodology</h3>
    <p>
      These instruments operate on a principle of coherence, not conformity. They do not enforce LALINE Doctrine unless that doctrine is explicitly declared as intent. They measure alignment between what was stated and what was built.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each instrument produces a verdict with rationale. The rationale cites specific observable signals that contradict declared intent. This is not opinion. It is evidence.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .page-meta {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .content-section p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .instruments-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .instrument-card {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .instrument-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .instrument-number {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    min-width: 2.5rem;
  }

  .instrument-card h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .instrument-card h2 a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .instrument-card h2 a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--text);
  }

  .instrument-description {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-left: 4.5rem;
  }

  .instrument-status {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--text);
    padding-left: 4.5rem;
  }

  .instrument-status.coming-soon {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .instruments-note {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 2rem;
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .instruments-note h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .instruments-note p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .instrument-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .instrument-description,
    .instrument-status {
      padding-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
